T7 — Download / processing instructions (TWO paths)

The 47 runs are NOT one dataset. Only the 20 dRNA-seq runs go through TSSpredator (T10);
the other 27 (Capp-Switch, 5' RNA-seq) use the papers' published TSS tables. See README.md
for the full rationale. (This supersedes the old single-list instructions, which downloaded
all 47 locally with fastq-dump.)

============================================================
PATH A — 20 dRNA-seq runs (C. difficile) -> TSSpredator (T10)
============================================================
Run this ON HPC4 (SuperPOD) — don't pull tens of GB to a laptop and re-upload. sra-tools is
already in the T4 conda env (prefetch, fasterq-dump).

  conda activate /project/igem2026/envs/promoter-mining-hpc4
  cd <work dir>            # on /project or /scratch (see T4/DEPLOY.md)

  # fetch only the 20 TSSpredator-compatible runs
  prefetch --option-file <repo>/data-acquisition-and-curation/tss-literature/SRR_dRNAseq_for_TSSpredator.txt
  for srr in $(cat <repo>/data-acquisition-and-curation/tss-literature/SRR_dRNAseq_for_TSSpredator.txt); do
      fasterq-dump --split-3 "$srr" -O . && gzip -f "${srr}"*.fastq
  done

  # then, in T10:
  #  - align to the CONFIRMED C. difficile assembly
  #    (630 = AM180355 / NC_009089; 630Delta-erm = its own assembly — see README)
  #  - build coverage/wiggle tracks
  #  - run TSSpredator with the correct TEX+/TEX- pairing (README verify-item #1)

============================================================
PATH B — 27 Capp-Switch + 5' RNA-seq runs -> published TSS tables
============================================================
Do NOT reprocess these with TSSpredator (they have no TEX- control). Use the supplementary
TSS tables from the papers and lift over to the matching in-genus assembly:

  - Hocq 2022 (Microbiol Spectr, doi:10.1128/spectrum.02288-21)
    C. acetobutylicum ATCC 824, C. beijerinckii NCIMB 8052 / DSM 6423 (~12,114 mapped TSS).
  - Al-Bassam 2018 (Nat Commun, doi:10.1038/s41467-018-06993-6)
    C. ljungdahlii ATCC 55383.

  (The raw runs stay in the per-method CSVs if a non-TSSpredator caller is ever needed.)

Tip: check installation with `fasterq-dump --version` (sra-tools).
